RopeTool known limitations / future work:

* Outer-join covers joint gaps up to ~80 degrees of bend per joint; beyond that
  the extended endpoints drift outside the discovery join tolerance and the
  chain splits. Extreme bends could use sphere joint parts instead.
* Closed-loop rope chains are detected (walk terminates) but the extracted
  chain may duplicate edges; loops aren't really editable yet.
* While dragging one endpoint handle, the other two handle sets (other
  endpoint + sag) don't re-render until the drag ends (selection sync is
  suppressed during drags). Cosmetic.
* Rope segments are built CanCollide = false; possibly worth a setting.
* No F-to-focus-selection key (PolyMap has one).
* A junction whose branches leave at similar shallow angles (within the 45
  degree attachment threshold on both sides, e.g. a sagging rope whose
  end-tangent aligns with the rope it attaches to) is ambiguous and still
  terminates the chain walk.
